Let \(H\) be a real Hilbert space, \(C\subset H\) nonempty, closed, and convex, and \(x\in H\), \(p\in C\). The following are equivalent:
\[
p=P_Cx;
\qquad \langle x-p,z-p\rangle\le0\quad(\forall z\in C);
\qquad x-p\in N_C(p);
\]
and these are also equivalent to
\[
\|x-z\|^2\ge\|x-p\|^2+\|p-z\|^2\quad(\forall z\in C).
\]

